{"title":"2012 USAMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_1\">Day 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Find all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/1/8f1e2533d6abdb11a9a1626c0240fab1a9200fc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> such that among any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> positive real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/6/64683f315744c851898c8d65dace1a8aa31b93ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dots$\" width=\"19\" height=\"2\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> with\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/e/ceee7231e7bcd541488519c12e11c9ff7478d0c3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\max(a_1, a_2, \\dots, a_n) \\le n \\cdot \\min(a_1, a_2, \\dots, a_n),\\]\" width=\"346\" height=\"18\" />\nthere exist three that are the side lengths of an acute triangle.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2012 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>A circle is divided into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/b/f0ba0869bc6d870183da454121b81794a5fdb166.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$432$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> congruent arcs by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/b/f0ba0869bc6d870183da454121b81794a5fdb166.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$432$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> points.  The points are colored in four colors such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/5/a75cef16b301d38a271625130c1aac46a7e9ce72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$108$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> points are colored red,  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/5/a75cef16b301d38a271625130c1aac46a7e9ce72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$108$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> points are colored green, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/5/a75cef16b301d38a271625130c1aac46a7e9ce72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$108$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> points are colored blue  and the remaining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/5/a75cef16b301d38a271625130c1aac46a7e9ce72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$108$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> points are colored yellow.  Prove that one can choose three points of each color in such a way that the four triangles formed by the chosen points of the same color are congruent.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2012 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Determine which integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/d/49d98ffe996c0f0d3b82b284cba2113439fefea9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> have the property that there exists an infinite sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/572b65ebc3f438b176b4ca4a890799f2f72564af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/6/64683f315744c851898c8d65dace1a8aa31b93ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dots$\" width=\"19\" height=\"2\" /> of nonzero integers such that the equality\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb59afa27abb3e054ab7f2cb301e50ffcca5ad62.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_k + 2a_{2k} + \\dots + na_{nk} = 0\\]\" width=\"208\" height=\"15\" />\nholds for every positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2012 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_2\">Day 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Find all functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/b/3dbce4e72ad7c1746623d1dfc9bbd46cad07cb91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f : \\mathbb{Z}^+ \\to \\mathbb{Z}^+$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" /> (where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/f/03fae0974b852c6df5091d7f45ca46d26429986a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{Z}^+$\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the set of positive integers) such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/d/23dc6c08a472f61de7cc4337c2a8fd614883ee17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n!) = f(n)!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"104\" height=\"18\" /> for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/d/39dd48954afea6461cb5f99e7d4d0cfb274cdc52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m - n$\" width=\"48\" height=\"8\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/f/03f4148177aeebb6883fddcfe5629cc633ac411f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(m) - f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" /> for all distinct positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2012 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be a point in the plane of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/66981fa3920210c6ad8dbe5e968783d5dd7520c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" /> a line passing through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/1090530ae883b627e090bfb5e450ef796febca40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c71f19552a05ee5e2b31e94aff3fb986884bf31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/7/9b798193cb94562989018728e1151587c618655b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"16\" /> be the points where the reflections of lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/7/377291318df52e4f013ab2bf28ee82454a9e57da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/9/9f988caff51f7fc88ad40d1d25022c52ffd8f976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/e/30e049532148caaf1c48e37658b548a6255c8d59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/66981fa3920210c6ad8dbe5e968783d5dd7520c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" /> intersect lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, respectively.  Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/1090530ae883b627e090bfb5e450ef796febca40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c71f19552a05ee5e2b31e94aff3fb986884bf31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/7/9b798193cb94562989018728e1151587c618655b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"16\" /> are collinear.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2012 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>For integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/7/317096889b84df0b72bf69ceb4c82208305f1b0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7d010bbff66a0c41e43310a51efbaa6bf63396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/6/64683f315744c851898c8d65dace1a8aa31b93ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dots$\" width=\"19\" height=\"2\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195db3e04ee69d85a0aeaedbb1cf9afa97ff4546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> be real numbers satisfying\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/9/8c9c8a3e2c9027abba620c84789f4c9f7586f6cc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_1 + x_2 + \\dots + x_n = 0, \\quad \\text{and} \\quad x_1^2 + x_2^2 + \\dots + x_n^2 = 1.\\]\" width=\"423\" height=\"19\" />\nFor each subset <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/c/27c953b6706f81ab1e46b6e765d03937e0c30f9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A \\subseteq \\{1, 2, \\dots, n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" />, define\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/7/45717db127bc90fec3df2da18ec709f9df5a8619.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S_A = \\sum_{i \\in A} x_i.\\]\" width=\"94\" height=\"39\" />\n(If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is the empty set, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/a/04abe8df443b3c5da24ba78c54b124ff7b9a8c8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_A = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" />.)\n</p><p>Prove that for any positive number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/4/ce4588fd900d02afcbd260bc07f54cce49a7dc4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda$\" width=\"10\" height=\"13\" />, the number of sets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/a/d3ad4e2fdd660d35b316cbd593ecd899c1de5367.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_A \\ge \\lambda$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" /> is at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/e/e7e289647937359a45ec83caaba588171b6773f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{n - 3}/\\lambda^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"19\" />.  For what choices of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7d010bbff66a0c41e43310a51efbaa6bf63396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/6/64683f315744c851898c8d65dace1a8aa31b93ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dots$\" width=\"19\" height=\"2\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195db3e04ee69d85a0aeaedbb1cf9afa97ff4546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/4/ce4588fd900d02afcbd260bc07f54cce49a7dc4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda$\" width=\"10\" height=\"13\" /> does equality hold?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2012 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO\" title=\"2012 USAMO\">2012 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2012\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO\" title=\"2011 USAMO\">2011 USAMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_USAMO\" title=\"2013 USAMO\">2013 USAMO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2012 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2012 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2012 